I reviewed C:/Users/purin/Downloads/game guide.docx. The core loop is understandable, but several rules need clarification before implementation. I have not changed the guide or started the next version.
The guide was modified October 4 at 22:39 and has no Git revision history. References below use its section names and card entries.
No winning condition or ending.
Key terms; How a cycle plays: losing at 0 Light is defined, but winning is not. Specify whether this is endless survival, a fixed number of cycles, or a delivery target. Also define what happens when no souls remain.
Setup and soul information are incomplete.
Choose passengers; Demo scope: specify initial shore population, new arrivals per cycle, whether delivered souls return, and each character’s seat cost and destination. The quest establishes Child → Haven and Mother → Tartarus, but the remaining destinations are unspecified.
The map can leave passengers without a delivery route.
New map; Drop off souls: delivery is allowed only at a preferred destination. Define map length, repeated destinations, whether required destinations are guaranteed, and what happens when the map ends with passengers aboard. Also specify how much of the map is visible before boarding, especially because foresight memories depend on hidden information.
Forced tainted arrivals conflict with boat capacity.
Seats; Tainted souls: the boat holds 4 seats, yet a tainted soul must board every 3 rounds. There is no rule for a full boat. Specify arrival timing and whether the three-round counter continues across cycles or resets.
PoLong’s effect mixes different timers.
Demo scope, PoLong: “Every 3 turns” and “for every 2 rounds it stays” could describe spawning and escalation, but that distinction is unclear. Separate its arrival rule from its debuff. Define when fog increases, whether increases accumulate, and how multiple PoLongs interact.
Memory effects need exact playable wording.
Memory; Demo scope: define when memories can be played, whether they are consumed, how many can be used together, and whether they persist between cycles. In particular:
“See the future +3”: reveal three rounds, destinations, or something else?
“Prevent Light Toll +1”: “Light Toll” is not defined. Does this block fog, wraith damage, or both?
“Prevent anger by 1”: which soul, which anger counter, and does it reduce existing anger or prevent an increase?
“Prevent 1 fog”: one crossing or a longer duration? Can effects stack?
Anger needs initialization and boarding rules.
Anger table: the limits of 2 Shore Anger and 4 Ship Anger are clear. Specify starting values and whether boarding resets anger, transfers it, or starts a separate Ship Anger counter. A newly forced passenger’s first anger increase also needs a defined timing.
The quest reward has unresolved interactions.
Quest pair story: clarify whether Child and Mother must be delivered in the same cycle, whether the special memory replaces or supplements Mother’s normal memory, and whether instant delivery earns the target’s ordinary memory or completes another quest.
Light recovery and return costs need explicit wording.
Light; Return to the shore; Haven row: starting Light is 6, but maximum Light is unspecified. State whether returning costs Light or counts as a round. Haven’s “free rest point” wording may suggest healing, although its listed effect only establishes fog 0.
Smaller corrections:
Replace “every 3 Cycle rounds” with the intended unit, and use round consistently instead of alternating with turn.
“1 soul of each memory type” conflicts with repeated effects: Merchant/Poet and Mason/Keeper. If intended, write “one of each listed soul.”
Add “except Child” to the general memory reward rule.
Add one worked round showing memory use, fog payment, delivery, tainted effects, and anger resolution.
The highest-priority decisions are the ending, map reachability, forced boarding, and memory definitions. This was a text and rules review; page layout and gameplay balance remain unverified.

